# 7. NASA DATA INTEGRATION: CRITICAL REQUIREMENT

This is one of the most important parts of KhetPatch.

Build actual, independently testable connectors for the NASA data sources below.

Do not substitute manually entered values or fictional API responses.

The system must retrieve available observations, process them, store them, relate them to the correct farm or field and use them in the application.

## 7.1 NASA GPM IMERG precipitation

Official source:

https://gpm.nasa.gov/data/imerg

Implement a connector for the appropriate GPM IMERG product and run.

Support the relevant product variants:

- Early Run.
- Late Run.
- Final Run.

Use the latest appropriate product collection available through the provider catalogue. Do not assume collection versions will never change.

Prioritise Early Run when low-latency precipitation information is required and it is genuinely available.

Retrieve precipitation data using official NASA/GES DISC or NASA Precipitation Processing System access routes and the applicable Earthdata authentication.

Implement provider discovery through NASA collection/granule metadata rather than relying on an unverified hardcoded file path.

Requirements:

- Search for granules covering the selected field.
- Retrieve the correct observation interval.
- Parse the actual raster or scientific data format.
- Decode the relevant variable.
- Interpret scale factors and units correctly.
- Apply quality and validity flags where provided.
- Calculate daily and selectable-period rainfall accumulation where the source product supports it.
- Preserve actual observation dates and product/run information.
- Store the original source reference.
- Display the relevant spatial resolution.

Use the product's correct precipitation semantics.

Never confuse precipitation rate with accumulated rainfall.

Do not aggregate rates as accumulated amounts without the correct temporal conversion.

## 7.2 NASA SMAP L4 soil moisture

Official source:

https://nsidc.org/data/smap

Primary product families:

- SPL4SMAU.
- SPL4SMGP.

Use the most appropriate current product and version discovered through official metadata.

SMAP L4 offers approximately 3-hourly soil-moisture estimates on a 9 km grid, but its public archive availability can lag the nominal observation interval.

Implement:

- Earthdata authentication.
- Collection and granule discovery.
- Download or supported remote subsetting.
- NetCDF/HDF data parsing.
- Surface soil-moisture extraction.
- Root-zone soil-moisture extraction where available.
- Correct physical units.
- Product quality flags.
- Geospatial intersection with selected farm/field geometry.
- Observation and publication timestamps.

Clearly explain that these values are regional gridded estimates, not direct field probes or laboratory soil tests.

Never display a field-level certainty that the native data resolution cannot support.

