## 7.4 Landsat 8 and Landsat 9

Official sources:

https://www.usgs.gov/landsat-missions/landsat-collection-2

https://www.usgs.gov/landsat-missions/landsat-data-access

Use Landsat 8/9 Collection 2 imagery, prioritising appropriate Level-2 surface-reflectance products where available.

Use official USGS/NASA data access and cataloguing mechanisms, such as supported STAC or Earthdata catalogue services.

Retrieve:

- Acquisition date.
- Satellite identifier.
- Scene identifier.
- Product identifier and collection.
- Cloud-cover metadata.
- Surface-reflectance bands.
- Quality-assurance bands.
- Product publication/processing date.

Implement actual raster processing.

Calculate NDVI using the scientifically appropriate red and near-infrared reflectance bands:

NDVI = (NIR - RED) / (NIR + RED)

Requirements:

- Apply product scale factors and offsets where specified.
- Mask cloud, cloud-shadow and invalid pixels.
- Respect QA_PIXEL and relevant QA/saturation flags.
- Handle missing and saturated pixels.
- Compute meaningful field statistics over valid pixels.
- Preserve valid-pixel proportion and cloud-related quality information.
- Display the original acquisition date.
- Retain the source product reference.

Do not confuse Landsat NDVI with direct soil-health measurement, nutrient measurement or crop diagnosis.

Do not extrapolate a current NDVI observation from an old image and describe it as live.

If there is no suitable recent cloud-free scene, clearly report that no suitable recent observation is available.

