## 7.8 Data-processing accuracy

A field may be much smaller than an underlying satellite data cell.

Therefore:

- Preserve native source resolution.
- Intersect the field boundary with source-grid geometry.
- Use suitable extraction or aggregation methods.
- Record the number of contributing pixels/cells.
- Record missing-pixel percentages.
- Preserve uncertainty and quality metadata when supplied.
- Avoid precision claims resulting from resampling.
- Explain when a product is too coarse for meaningful field-level differentiation.

